        "watchBalance": [
            {
                "description": "rest snapshot arriving after a ws delta merges into the live balance object - the delta wins, the snapshot-only currency joins the aggregates, and the object handed to the consumer keeps its identity (frames and rest response reproduce the documented examples - no live keys for this venue)",
                "disabledPHP": "the php runtime starts a spawned coroutine synchronously, so loadBalanceSnapshot runs to completion against the instant mocked rest response before watchBalance registers its future - the dropped resolve leaves the watch pending (live rest responses arrive asynchronously, so real usage does not hit this order)",
                "disabledCS": "the spawned loadBalanceSnapshot may run to completion against the instant mocked rest response before watchBalance registers its future (thread-pool scheduling race) - the dropped resolve then leaves the watch pending, so the lane would flake",
                "disabledGO": "the spawned loadBalanceSnapshot goroutine may run to completion against the instant mocked rest response before watchBalance registers its future (scheduling race) - the dropped resolve then leaves the watch pending, so the lane would flake",
                "disabledJava": "the java static-ws harness never runs the spawned loadBalanceSnapshot against the mocked rest response, so the snapshot seed that resolves the watch never happens - rest seeding is covered by the other lanes",
                "disabledRS": "the rust static-ws harness does not route the mocked rest response into the spawned loadBalanceSnapshot task, so the snapshot seed that resolves the watch never happens - rest seeding is covered by the other lanes",
